<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Grove half year div rises, still in talks.</title>
<headline>Grove half year div rises, still in talks.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income		9.74	  vs 10.44</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 24.36	 vs 22.80</p>
<p>    Distrib income	  9.74	  vs 9.12</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.95	  vs 1.36</p>
<p>    Turnover		  12.82	 vs 12.14</p>
<p>Div payable October 30</p>
<p>on register October 18</p>
<p>Full name: Grove Property Fund Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it was still in talks that could have an effect on its share price and shareholders should exercise caution when dealing in its shares.</p>
<p>It added that earnings for the second period are expected to show a similar rate on increase as in the first.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
